{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1000", "sample_idx": 44, "model_name": "meta/llama-3.1-8b-instruct", "content": "Raymond III Count of Tripoli was a member of the House of Tripoli and the Count of Tripoli from 1152 until his death in 1187. He was the son of Raymond II Count of Tripoli and Hodierna of Jerusalem. His family had held the County of Tripoli since its founding by Raymond I in 1104.\n\n* **Early Life** *\nRaymond III was born in 1140 and was the son of Raymond II Count of Tripoli and Hodierna of Jerusalem. His mother was a member of the royal family of Jerusalem and was the sister of King Baldwin III of Jerusalem. He received his early education in the kingdom of Jerusalem.\n\nIn 1152 Raymond III succeeded his father as the Count of Tripoli. He faced challenges from the Muslim forces of Nur ad-Din who sought to conquer the County of Tripoli. Raymond III married a woman named Eschiva of Arsur in 1152 but she died shortly after giving birth to their son Bohemond.\n\n* **Conflict with Nur ad-Din** *\nIn 1164 Raymond III allied himself with the Crusader forces of King Amalric I of Jerusalem to fight against Nur ad-Din. The Crusaders were defeated and Nur ad-Din captured King Amalric I's sister Sibylla. Raymond III was forced to pay a ransom for her release.\n\nIn 1177 Raymond III and the Muslim forces of Saladin signed a treaty which included a mutual non-aggression pact. However the treaty did not last long and in 1187 Raymond III was captured by Saladin during the Siege of Tripoli.\n\n* **Death and Succession** *\nRaymond III was taken captive by Saladin and was eventually released in exchange for a large ransom. He died in 1187. His son Bohemond succeeded him as the Count of Tripoli but was killed in 1189 by the Muslim forces of Saladin.", "logprobs": [{"token": "Ray", "logprob": -0.014390614}, {"token": "mond", "logprob": -0.00016938205}, {"token": " III", "logprob": -0.0010648064}, {"token": " Count", "logprob": -0.1300828}, {"token": " of", "logprob":